    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d327">

                <pb facs="0500" n="1964" xml:id="pg1964"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">6S9.90D/4–2151: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Pakistan</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Warren</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">niact</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Karachi</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1951-04-21T14:00:00+05:30">April 21, 1951—2
                            p. m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>988. For McGhee. Re Embs 960, Apr 14.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d327-f1"/> PriMin in
                    conversation this p. m. hoped his reply ref Deptel 661, Apr 18 wld be considered
                    as an acceptance of the US Nov 6 <hi rendition="#italic">démarche</hi> and
                    regretted its unfavorable reception. After lengthy discussion based largely on
                    his recollection of conversation with McGhee and an exposition of the points in
                    Deptel under ref, the PriMin authorized me to say his govt accepts para 3 (b) of
                    Dept’s proposal, i.e. Pak accepts unconditionally first three points of US
                    approach of Nov 6 and reaffirms its attitude on point four of the Nov 6 approach
                    as expressed in its memo of Apr 14.</p>
                <p>Shld the Dept still consider this reaffirmation a counterproposal he nevertheless
                    wld be pleased to have the Dept submit it to the Afghans and wld welcome the
                    Dept’s indication of their reaction to it.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Warren</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
